{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And the sense of וככה תאכלו אותו (thus shall you eat it) is the Egyptian Passover alone. And the sects who are in Argilan do thus to this day as a remembrance of the exodus from Egypt — and all these wanderers of spirit go on the fifteenth day from their land as a remembrance of the exodus from Egypt." "<b>And your staffs in your hands.</b> To drive the donkeys, as in ויך את האתון במקל (and he struck the donkey with the staff) (Numbers 22:27)." "And the sense of בחפזון (in haste) is that they should not delay and should eat it quickly before the moment of the destroyer arrives, when HaShem passes over the threshold; therefore HaShem commanded that it be fire-roasted so it cooks quickly. And so the holy fathers said: it is eaten only until midnight, and it is eaten only roasted."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Reading 'בארגלן' as Argilan (i.e., Aragon/Catalonia region); the passage polemicizes against certain sectarians whose practices Ibn Ezra describes dismissively."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:33.539198251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}